From fd13be890b60e32302f0486ef607d90a95e9a8c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:37:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] facilitator-local: report a request for an unsupported
 network as invalid_network
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A /verify or /settle request for a network no handler serves (for example
eip155:1 on a facilitator configured for other chains) was answered with
unsupported_scheme. x402 v2 §9 has a code for that case, invalid_network:
"Specified blockchain network is not supported".

- SchemeRegistry::supports_chain tells whether any handler serves a chain.
- When no handler matches, FacilitatorLocal reports UnsupportedChain if the
  request's network is not served at all, and UnsupportedScheme otherwise (a
  served network without the requested scheme or version, or a request that
  names no network).
- PaymentVerificationError::UnsupportedChain, which scheme handlers already use
  for networks they cannot serve, now maps to the new ErrorReason::InvalidNetwork
  (invalid_network) instead of the non-spec unsupported_chain.
